										"Events": [],
										"Text":
										{
											"$text": "# UICS COASTAL NETWORK â€“ PORT NODE OSK-3 â€“ README\n\nYou are connected to Port Node OSK-3, the UICS terminal for the ports of Outskirts island.\n\nWhen government control collapsed, every faction took a piece of the island. The UICS holds the ports, and from here the coastal network is meant to expand inland. This node coordinates harbor traffic, the UICS general supply warehouses and the coastal patrols. Its uplink runs through the Comms Building complex on the hill.\n\n## SYSTEM FUNCTIONS\n\n- **read** Open and view a file's contents\n- **run** Execute a terminal-compatible program\n- **scan** Check a file for classification markers or hidden data\n- **download** â€“ Copy a file from the node to your local device\n\nUse `help` at any time for the full command list.\n\n## CLEARANCE LEVELS\n\n- Guest: Bulletins and public notices only\n- Quartermaster: Warehouse stock, harbor and vehicle maintenance records\n- Admin: Port command, defense orders and node configuration\n\n## STANDING ORDERS\n\n- Credentials are personal. Every session is logged against the account that opened it.\n- Encrypted intercept volumes open only with a matching Defense intel key. The node reports every failed attempt to Port Command.\n- If the node is compromised, shut it down and fall back to the harbor gate.\n\nUICS Order. Stability. Control.\n\n> END OF FILE",
											"$ns": "[2C9853E6E633F3D3F51C087FCE244600]",
											"$key": "88E1B74F4958E427F41D64B3B2D05490"
										}
									}
								]
							}
						}
					},
					{
